### Workout Logging API: every call the README shows.
###
### Open this file in VS Code (REST Client extension) or an editor with an
### .http runner, with `docker compose up` running. Send each request with
### its "Send Request" link. Three requests read a value from an earlier one
### (`{{logOne.response.body.data.id}}` and the cursor of `firstPage`), so
### send those first; the `{{name.response.body…}}` form is the REST Client
### extension's. Every date below is a full date-time with an offset, as
### the API requires.

@host = http://localhost:3000
@user = u_123

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Health and docs (unversioned)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Liveness: the process is up
GET {{host}}/health/live

### Readiness: the database answers
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### The OpenAPI document (the Swagger UI is at {{host}}/docs)
GET {{host}}/docs-json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Reference data
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Supported units and their aliases
GET {{host}}/v1/units

### The known muscle groups, each with the number of exercises that list it
GET {{host}}/v1/muscle-groups

### The catalog: every exercise with its muscle groups
GET {{host}}/v1/exercises

### One catalog exercise (the key is the normalised name)
GET {{host}}/v1/exercises/bench%20press

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Log entries
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Log one entry. 225 lb and 105 kg in one entry; 05:30 in Vietnam (+07:00).
### The response has the instant in UTC, the offset for display, kilograms and
### each set's original. The Location header points at the entry.
# @name logOne
POST {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/workout-entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2025-02-10T05:30:00+07:00",
  "exerciseName": "Bench Press",
  "sets": [
    { "reps": 5, "weight": 225, "unit": "lbs" },
    { "reps": 3, "weight": 105, "unit": "kg" }
  ]
}

### A client that sends UTC gets utcOffset null
POST {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/workout-entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2025-02-12T12:30:00Z",
  "exerciseName": "Bench Press",
  "sets": [
    { "reps": 10, "weight": 100, "unit": "kg" },
    { "reps": 2, "weight": 120, "unit": "kg" }
  ]
}

### Log several entries at once, atomically (1 to 100). The response lists them
### in the order sent; history lists them newest first.
POST {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/workout-entries/bulk
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "entries": [
    {
      "date": "2025-02-14T12:00:00+07:00",
      "exerciseName": "Back Squat",
      "sets": [
        { "reps": 5, "weight": 140, "unit": "kg" },
        { "reps": 5, "weight": 150, "unit": "kg" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "date": "2025-02-14T12:00:00+07:00",
      "exerciseName": "Pull-Up",
      "sets": [
        { "reps": 10, "weight": 0, "unit": "kg" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### One entry by id, here in pounds
GET {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/workout-entries/{{logOne.response.body.data.id}}?unit=lb

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Mistakes the API explains (each is a 4xx with problem details)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### A date alone is a 400 that shows the fix (400)
POST {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/workout-entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2025-02-10",
  "exerciseName": "Bench Press",
  "sets": [ { "reps": 5, "weight": 100, "unit": "kg" } ]
}

### An unsupported unit and a date-time with no offset: both errors at once (400)
POST {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/workout-entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2025-02-10T06:30:00",
  "exerciseName": "Bench Press",
  "sets": [ { "reps": 5, "weight": 100, "unit": "stone" } ]
}

### A body that is not JSON (what `curl -d` sends with no -H) is a 415
POST {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/workout-entries
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

date=2025-02-10T05:30:00%2B07:00&exerciseName=Bench%20Press

### A query parameter the route does not accept is a 400 that lists the accepted ones
GET {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/workout-entries?exerciseName=bench

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### History
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Newest first, a page of 2. Send it, then use the cursor in the next request.
# @name firstPage
GET {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/workout-entries?limit=2

### The next page: send the cursor unchanged
GET {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/workout-entries?limit=2&cursor={{firstPage.response.body.page.nextCursor}}

### Filters: part of the name, a muscle group, a range (half-open: from is
### included, to is excluded), weights shown in pounds. This range is February
### for a viewer in Hanoi.
GET {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/workout-entries?exercise=bench&muscleGroup=chest&from=2025-01-31T17:00:00Z&to=2025-02-28T17:00:00Z&unit=lb&limit=20

### No match is a 200 with an empty list and a message, not an error
GET {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/workout-entries?exercise=nothing-like-this

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Personal records
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Records for one exercise, all time. exercise is the whole name.
GET {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/personal-records?exercise=Bench%20Press

### The same in a range, in pounds
GET {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/personal-records?exercise=Bench%20Press&from=2025-02-01T00:00:00Z&to=2025-03-01T00:00:00Z&unit=lb

### Part of a name finds nothing here: a 200 with null records and a hint
GET {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/personal-records?exercise=bench

### This period against the one before it, with the change in each record.
### All four bounds are required; to is excluded, and this period's start is
### the other's end.
GET {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/personal-records/compare?exercise=Bench%20Press&from=2025-02-01T00:00:00Z&to=2025-03-01T00:00:00Z&compareFrom=2025-01-01T00:00:00Z&compareTo=2025-02-01T00:00:00Z&unit=kg

### A missing bound is one 400 that lists every missing parameter
GET {{host}}/v1/users/{{user}}/personal-records/compare?exercise=Bench%20Press&from=2025-02-01T00:00:00Z

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Catalog administration: THESE FIVE CALLS ARE OPEN.
### In the version as delivered they are unauthenticated: anyone who can
### reach the API can change the catalog. See the README, "Catalog
### administration", for the two lines that switch the token guard on. When
### it is on, add this header to each call:
###   Authorization: Bearer <the value of ADMIN_API_TOKEN>
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Add an exercise (201 with Location; 409 if its key exists)
POST {{host}}/v1/admin/exercises
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zercher Squat", "muscleGroups": ["quads", "glutes", "back"] }

### A key can contain a slash: Location is /v1/exercises/90%2F90%20hip%20stretch
POST {{host}}/v1/admin/exercises
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "90/90 Hip Stretch", "muscleGroups": ["glutes"] }

### Follow that Location
GET {{host}}/v1/exercises/90%2F90%20hip%20stretch

### Replace the muscle groups of an exercise (a full replacement; the name may
### change its spelling but not its key)
PUT {{host}}/v1/admin/exercises/zercher%20squat
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zercher Squat", "muscleGroups": ["quads", "glutes", "back", "abs"] }

### Remove an exercise from the catalog (204). Logged entries are not touched.
DELETE {{host}}/v1/admin/exercises/90%2F90%20hip%20stretch

### Add a muscle group to the closed list (201; 409 if it exists)
POST {{host}}/v1/admin/muscle-groups
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "neck" }

### Remove a muscle group that no exercise lists (204; 409 while one does)
DELETE {{host}}/v1/admin/muscle-groups/neck
